# ============================================================
# OPEP monorepo .dockerignore
# Goal: ship the smallest possible Docker build context.
# Patterns are gitignore-style (Docker supports the same syntax).
#
# ⚠️ CRITICAL: NEVER exclude `apps/web/app/reproduction/**/*.tsx` or
# `apps/client/src/pages/reproduction/**/*.tsx` — those are runtime
# Next.js / Vite routes. Excluding them would silently drop them
# from the output bundle. Only the auto-generated AI integration
# guides (`*.prompt.md`) and one-off root scripts are safe to hide.
# ============================================================

# --- VCS / metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Dependencies (always installed fresh in deps stage) ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Build outputs (produced inside the deps/builder stages) ---
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.nuxt
**/.svelte-kit
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/.parcel-cache

# --- Test artifacts ---
coverage
**/coverage
**/*.lcov
.nyc_output
junit.xml
**/jest-cache

# --- Logs / runtime junk ---
*.log
logs
**/logs
**/*.log-*

# --- Secrets / local env (NEVER ship a real .env in CI) ---
# `**/` widens the net so .env files under apps/, packages/ and any other
# sub-tree cannot accidentally leak into a published image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets/**
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# --- TypeScript build info + linter caches ---
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.prettiercache

# --- Editor / IDE / OS metadata ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Docker / orchestration --- (these files don't belong in the image)
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.dockerignore
.hadolint.yaml

# --- Documentation (humans only, useless at runtime) ---
*.md
README.md
LICENSE
docs
**/docs
docs-md
skills
**/skills

# --- Auto-generated AI integration guides ---
# We deleted 60 .prompt.md files plus their generators earlier; the glob
# is kept as a safety net should anyone re-run the reproduction pipeline.
# Note: generate-keys.js, the QR-signing-keys helper, is at the repo root
# and is intentionally included in the build context. It prints to stdout
# and the actual keys are wired in via env vars (QR_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY /
# QR_SIGNING_PUBLIC_KEY) consumed at runtime by @opep/qr-utils.
**/*.prompt.md

# --- Cypress / Playwright / E2E caches ---
**/cypress/videos
**/cypress/screenshots
**/.playwright

# --- Local Postgres / MAMP data dumps (host dev data, never the API runtime) ---
**/mamp
**/phpMyAdmin
